    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Georgetown’s settlement dates to the 1720s, making it one of Connecticut’s oldest villages.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.georgetownct.org/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Gilbert & Bennett wire mill operated from 1818 to 1989, shaping Georgetown’s industrial heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.georgetownct.org/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After closing in the late 1980s, Georgetown reclaimed the mill in 2021 and is remediating it for new uses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.georgetownct.org/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Georgetown Historic District earned National Register status in 1987, preserving its 90‑acre core of historic buildings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgetown%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Georgetown sits at the junction of Wilton, Redding, and Weston, anchoring a unique tri‑town community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgetown%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A self‑guided walking tour lets visitors explore Georgetown’s historic streets and learn its stories firsthand.",
